gcm/live-draw: main-memory render targets reach guest memory at sync points; guest writes behind live-draw are seen.

Symptom (Killzone 3, pass 19): live-draw keeps render targets on the GPU and caches textures by a content hash
taken once per frame. Guest memory is also written outside the FIFO: KZ3 copies its scene target to main memory
(NV0039, patch 2015), its SPU post jobs process that copy, and the final composite samples main 0x1310400 plus a
160x90 main-memory image (RPCS3 capture, both level captures). A guest write into the memory of a live colour
surface was never seen (texture binds that resolve to the surface sampled the stale GPU copy), and a write into an
already-hashed texture within the same frame was seen only at the next flip.

Second symptom (same captures): right after the copy KZ3 renders four colour surfaces in MAIN memory (640x360
0x16D0400 and 320x180 0x19AB800 scene downsamples, 640x360 0x1892400 from depth, 320x180 F_X32 0x1A1C000), then
releases a semaphore for its SPU post jobs. live-draw kept those pixels on the GPU, so the SPUs read stale memory.

Fix:
- Main-memory colour surfaces the GPU drew since their last write-back are written back into guest memory (RSX
  layout, the patch 2015 path, now ld_writeback_surface) before the guest can observe a sync point: NV4097
  0x1D70/0x1D74 semaphore release (rsx_commands.c), NV406E 0x6C release (cellGcmSys.c), flip.
  rsx_live_draw_before_guest_sync(); LD_MAIN_SURFACE_WRITEBACK=0 disables.
- Live colour surfaces (RGBA8, FP16, F_X32): a sampled hash of the guest bytes per band of 16 rows. Baseline after
  GPU writes (first texture bind or the flip); at most one compare per frame when the surface is bound as a
  texture; changed bands are converted to the host layout (inverse of the patch 2015 write-back) and uploaded into
  the surface before the draw. LD_GUEST_HASH_STRIDE (default 1024: one 64-byte chunk per 1 KB per row, phase
  stepping so a band's 16 rows cover every chunk column; 0 = whole rows). An NV0039 write-back first takes guest
  bytes that are newer than the GPU's, then re-baselines.
- Exact path: rsx_live_draw_note_guest_write (rsx thread) now also marks the written rows of live surfaces;
  rsx_live_draw_note_guest_write_async (any thread, lock-free ring drained before texture binds) and
  cellGcm_note_guest_write_ea(ea, size) (EA -> local offset or IO offset) are the hook for SPU DMA puts.
- LD_GUEST_WRITE_DBG=1: [guest-write] lines say whether an NV0039 copy destination was rewritten between the copy
  and the next texture bind that reads it (KZ3: did the SPU post chain run before the composite).
- [guest-validate] cost line every 300 frames (KB hashed and microseconds per frame). LD_GUEST_WRITE_CHECK=0 = off.

Verified: tools/smoke/test_guest_write.c under Proton (cases S, N, H, T, M; PASS; negative controls
LD_GUEST_WRITE_CHECK=0 and LD_MAIN_SURFACE_WRITEBACK=0 FAIL); test_nv0039, test_surface_aa, test_tex_float PASS.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.17.0 (SPU pass 95): the 0x6C RELEASE keeps #401's get publish + fence after the live-draw sync; 0x1D70/74 sync before #381's FEED0001 path; #395's swin fields kept.

